/* =========================================================================
   JUNI  —  physical focus timer UI
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Hardware : ESP32-S3 (N16R8, PSRAM)  +  240x320 SPI TFT (ST7789)  +  rotary
   Framework: Arduino

   Wiring (DO NOT CHANGE)
     TFT CS  -> 10      ENC S1  -> 6
     TFT RST -> 9       ENC S2  -> 7
     TFT DC  -> 4       ENC KEY -> 8
     TFT SDA -> 11
     TFT SCK -> 12

   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   SECTION MAP
     1  Configuration & pins
     2  Types            <-- ALL structs/enums/classes live here, see note
     3  Colour + math helpers
     4  Framebuffer flush
     5  Antialiased drawing primitives
     6  Screen layout constants
     7  Panda expression data
     8  Panda renderer    (the ONLY place that knows about pixels)
     9  Text engine       (supersampled, scalable, antialiased numerals)
    10  UI layers         (panda / timer / status dot)
    11  Application state machine
    12  Input             (encoder + button)
    13  Countdown
    14  Animation update
    15  Render orchestration (layer dirty model)
    16  setup() / loop()

   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   WHY EVERY TYPE IS DECLARED IN SECTION 2

   The Arduino IDE auto-generates function prototypes and injects them
   immediately before the FIRST function definition in the .ino file. Any
   struct or enum declared after that point is invisible to those generated
   prototypes, which fails with "'Rect' does not name a type".

   So: section 2 contains every type and NO function definitions. Do not add
   a function definition above it.
   ========================================================================= */

